<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:controls="clr-namespace:KinesisEdit.Controls"
             xmlns:views="clr-namespace:KinesisEdit.Views"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:KinesisEdit.ViewModels"
             xmlns:model="clr-namespace:KinesisEdit.Core.Model;assembly=KinesisEdit.Core"
             mc:Ignorable="d" d:DesignWidth="960" d:DesignHeight="560"
             x:Class="KinesisEdit.Views.MacroLibraryView"
             x:DataType="vm:MacroLibraryViewModel">
  <!--
    The Macros tab (mockup 1i), which is a LIBRARY and not an editor: "every macro has a name, so
    the tab lists them once — rename, see which keys and layers fire each one, duplicate, delete"
    (2i). Editing a macro happens on the key inspector rail beside the board.

    ONE VIEW, TWO BRANCHES, PICKED BY THE CAPABILITY RECORD. `UsesMacroSlots` draws 1i's left half
    (the selected key's slot cards, its two meters and its `Pick another key`) and
    `UsesFlatMacroList` its right (the Advantage 360's flat table with its `Macro / Trigger / Layer /
    Length` columns and `New macro`). There is no device-specific view and no device id anywhere in
    this file — a feature a board lacks is not rendered at all.

    THE TABLE IS THE SAME ROWS ON BOTH BRANCHES. `Rows` is one row per library entry, so a macro on
    two keys is one row with two sites, whichever branch is drawn. The slot branch heads it "Every
    macro in this profile"; the flat branch heads it with 1i's four column captions.

    NOTHING HERE CAPTURES A KEYSTROKE. `＋ Record a macro` and `New macro` both leave for the Layout
    tab, where the board and the app's one recording surface are. Mockup 1i draws a capture-mode
    overlay on this tab; not building it is a deliberate deviation, recorded in
    docs/app/design-system.md.

    MONO IS THE FILE'S VOICE. The keystrokes, the trigger tokens and the lengths are values that
    exist verbatim in layoutN.txt or are counted against it; a macro's NAME is not — it rides
    app_settings.txt and is the app speaking — so it is sans.
  -->
  <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,*,Auto">

    <!-- ===== The header ======================================================================
         "Macros on F3 · Freestyle Edge RGB" / "3 of 5 slots used · 1 active" / "Pick another key",
         or the flat branch's own three. -->
    <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="12" Margin="0,0,0,12">
      <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="2">
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding Header}" Classes="pageTitle" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding Subtitle}" Classes="meta muted" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
      </StackPanel>

      <Button Grid.Column="1"
              Classes="secondary"
              Content="{Binding PrimaryActionCaption}"
              Command="{Binding PrimaryActionCommand}"
              IsVisible="{Binding IsSupported}"
              VerticalAlignment="Center" />
    </Grid>

    <!-- ===== The refusal =====================================================================
         Drawn INSTEAD of the tab's contents. A board with no macros at all still carries this tab
         (the strip is built from device facts before a profile is read), so the tab says so itself
         rather than rendering an empty library. Amber, never red — nothing failed. -->
    <Border Grid.Row="1"
            Background="{DynamicResource StatusAdvisoryTintBrush}"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource StatusAdvisoryTintBorderBrush}"
            BorderThickness="1"
            CornerRadius="{DynamicResource RadiusControl}"
            Padding="9,7"
            IsVisible="{Binding !IsSupported}">
      <TextBlock Text="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.NotSupportedMessage}"
                 Classes="body statusWarning"
                 TextWrapping="Wrap" />
    </Border>

    <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="2" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled" IsVisible="{Binding IsSupported}">
      <StackPanel Spacing="16">

        <!-- ===== The slot cards ==============================================================
             1i's left half: "Slot 1 — Sign-off block" with its keystrokes, badged ACTIVE or
             offering `Make active`; "Slot 4 — empty" offering `＋ Record a macro`; and the
             over-budget slot carrying its amber sentence, which changes nothing else about it.

             The card is a Border with a pointer handler rather than a Button, because it holds
             buttons of its own and a button nested in a button fires both commands on one click. -->
        <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Slots}" IsVisible="{Binding HasSlots}">
          <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
            <ItemsPanelTemplate>
              <StackPanel Spacing="8" />
            </ItemsPanelTemplate>
          </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
          <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            <DataTemplate DataType="vm:MacroSlotViewModel">
              <Border Classes="macroSlotCard"
                      Classes.selected="{Binding IsSelected}"
                      PointerPressed="OnSlotPointerPressed">
                <StackPanel Spacing="6">
                  <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0"
                               Text="{Binding Title}"
                               Classes="cardTitle"
                               TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" />

                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                      <!-- The accent means "this is the one selected" in its second sanctioned
                           sense: which macro the key actually fires. -->
                      <TextBlock Text="{x:Static vm:MacroSlotViewModel.ActiveBadge}"
                                 Classes="badge"
                                 IsVisible="{Binding IsActive}"
                                 VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                      <Button Classes="secondary"
                              Content="{x:Static vm:MacroSlotViewModel.MakeActiveCaption}"
                              IsVisible="{Binding CanMakeActive}"
                              Command="{Binding $parent[views:MacroLibraryView].((vm:MacroLibraryViewModel)DataContext).MakeActiveCommand}"
                              CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                    </StackPanel>
                  </Grid>

                  <TextBlock Text="{Binding KeystrokesText}"
                             Classes="monoValue"
                             TextWrapping="Wrap"
                             IsVisible="{Binding IsOccupied}" />

                  <!-- "512 of 500 characters — over the device budget. Saved as-is." Amber, and the
                       whole consequence: the macro keeps its slot and the profile still saves. -->
                  <TextBlock Text="{Binding BudgetAdvisory}"
                             Classes="body statusWarning"
                             TextWrapping="Wrap"
                             IsVisible="{Binding IsOverBudget}" />

                  <!-- The `＋` is geometry (IconInsert), never a character: U+FF0B is in neither
                       embedded IBM Plex family and would tofu. -->
                  <Button Classes="secondary"
                          HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                          IsVisible="{Binding IsEmpty}"
                          Command="{Binding $parent[views:MacroLibraryView].((vm:MacroLibraryViewModel)DataContext).RecordMacroCommand}"
                          CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
                      <controls:Icon Classes="insertMark" Data="{DynamicResource IconInsert}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                      <TextBlock Text="{x:Static vm:MacroSlotViewModel.RecordCaption}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </StackPanel>
                  </Button>
                </StackPanel>
              </Border>
            </DataTemplate>
          </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
        </ItemsControl>

        <StackPanel Spacing="8">
          <!-- The slot branch's heading over the profile's whole library. The flat branch heads the
               same rows with 1i's column captions instead. -->
          <TextBlock Text="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.LibrarySectionTitle}"
                     Classes="cardTitle"
                     IsVisible="{Binding UsesMacroSlots}" />

          <!-- ===== Search and the layer filter ===============================================
               `⌕ Search name, trigger, or contents…` and `All layers ▾`. The magnifier belongs to
               the SearchField control theme and the chevron to the ComboBox's; neither is a glyph.
               Both filters narrow the rows and write nothing. -->
          <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
            <TextBox Grid.Column="0"
                     Classes="searchField"
                     Watermark="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.SearchPlaceholder}"
                     Text="{Binding SearchQuery, Mode=TwoWay}" />
            <ComboBox Grid.Column="1"
                      MinWidth="150"
                      ItemsSource="{Binding LayerFilters}"
                      SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedLayerFilter, Mode=TwoWay}">
              <ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                <DataTemplate DataType="vm:MacroLayerFilter">
                  <TextBlock Text="{Binding Caption}" />
                </DataTemplate>
              </ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
            </ComboBox>
          </Grid>

          <!-- 1i's column captions. Drawn on the flat branch, which is where the mock puts them;
               the columns themselves are in every row on both branches. -->
          <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto,Auto"
                ColumnSpacing="12"
                Margin="0,4,0,0"
                IsVisible="{Binding UsesFlatMacroList}">
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.MacroColumnCaption}" Classes="sectionLabel" />
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.TriggerColumnCaption}" Classes="sectionLabel" MinWidth="120" />
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.LayerColumnCaption}" Classes="sectionLabel" MinWidth="70" />
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Text="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.LengthColumnCaption}" Classes="sectionLabel" MinWidth="48" />
          </Grid>

          <!-- ===== One row per macro, by name ================================================
               Not a walk over the keys: MacroLibrary.Entries is the answer to "which keys and
               layers fire this one", and a macro on two keys is one row with two sites. -->
          <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Rows}">
            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
              <DataTemplate DataType="vm:MacroLibraryRowViewModel">
                <Border Classes="listRow">
                  <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="12">
                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="3">
                      <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}"
                                 Classes="rowCaption"
                                 IsVisible="{Binding !IsRenaming}" />

                      <!-- Renaming in place. A blank name CLEARS the stored one, which is why the
                           field is allowed to be empty; MacroNaming bounds its length, so the box
                           does too rather than letting Core silently truncate what was typed. -->
                      <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                                  Spacing="6"
                                  IsVisible="{Binding IsRenaming}">
                        <TextBox MinWidth="180"
                                 MaxLength="{x:Static model:MacroNaming.MaxNameLength}"
                                 Watermark="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.RenameWatermark}"
                                 Text="{Binding RenameText, Mode=TwoWay}" />
                        <Button Classes="primaryAction"
                                Content="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.SaveNameCaption}"
                                Command="{Binding $parent[views:MacroLibraryView].((vm:MacroLibraryViewModel)DataContext).CommitRenameCommand}"
                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                        <Button Classes="secondary"
                                Content="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.CancelRenameCaption}"
                                Command="{Binding $parent[views:MacroLibraryView].((vm:MacroLibraryViewModel)DataContext).CancelRenameCommand}"
                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                      </StackPanel>

                      <TextBlock Text="{Binding ContentsText}"
                                 Classes="monoValueSmall muted"
                                 TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />

                      <!-- "Fires from [f3] · Fn, [f7] · Fn" — said only when there is more than one
                           place, because the Trigger and Layer columns already name the first. -->
                      <TextBlock Text="{Binding SitesText}"
                                 Classes="meta muted"
                                 TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                 IsVisible="{Binding HasSeveralSites}" />

                      <TextBlock Text="{Binding BudgetAdvisory}"
                                 Classes="body statusWarning"
                                 TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                 IsVisible="{Binding IsOverBudget}" />

                      <!-- Ghost, not link: four affordances per row in the accent colour would
                           spend the accent on something that is neither selection nor "you changed
                           this" (docs/design/README.md). -->
                      <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="2" IsVisible="{Binding !IsRenaming}">
                        <Button Classes="ghost"
                                Content="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.EditCaption}"
                                Command="{Binding $parent[views:MacroLibraryView].((vm:MacroLibraryViewModel)DataContext).EditMacroCommand}"
                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                        <Button Classes="ghost"
                                Content="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.RenameCaption}"
                                Command="{Binding $parent[views:MacroLibraryView].((vm:MacroLibraryViewModel)DataContext).BeginRenameCommand}"
                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                        <Button Classes="ghost"
                                Content="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.DuplicateCaption}"
                                Command="{Binding $parent[views:MacroLibraryView].((vm:MacroLibraryViewModel)DataContext).DuplicateCommand}"
                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                        <Button Classes="ghost"
                                Content="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.DeleteCaption}"
                                Command="{Binding $parent[views:MacroLibraryView].((vm:MacroLibraryViewModel)DataContext).DeleteCommand}"
                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                      </StackPanel>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                               Text="{Binding TriggerText}"
                               Classes="monoValue"
                               MinWidth="120"
                               TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               VerticalAlignment="Top" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2"
                               Text="{Binding LayerText}"
                               Classes="meta muted"
                               MinWidth="70"
                               TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               VerticalAlignment="Top" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="3"
                               Text="{Binding LengthText}"
                               Classes="monoValue"
                               Classes.statusWarning="{Binding IsOverBudget}"
                               MinWidth="48"
                               VerticalAlignment="Top" />
                  </Grid>
                </Border>
              </DataTemplate>
            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
          </ItemsControl>

          <TextBlock Text="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.NoMacrosMessage}"
                     Classes="body muted"
                     IsVisible="{Binding IsEmpty}" />
          <TextBlock Text="{x:Static vm:MacroLibraryViewModel.NoMatchesMessage}"
                     Classes="body muted"
                     IsVisible="{Binding HasNoMatches}" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- What the tab refused, and why. Amber: a full slot strip is a fact about the profile,
             not a failure. -->
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding Message}"
                   Classes="body statusWarning"
                   TextWrapping="Wrap"
                   IsVisible="{Binding HasMessage}" />
      </StackPanel>
    </ScrollViewer>

    <!-- ===== The meters ======================================================================
         1i's two, in its words — "layout keystroke budget 5 140 / 7 200" and "this macro 512 / 500"
         — plus the macro count, which is the only place the profile's 06 §6 limit is readable now
         that the old panel's budget block is gone. Over budget goes AMBER and still saves. -->
    <StackPanel Grid.Row="3" Spacing="4" Margin="0,12,0,0" IsVisible="{Binding IsSupported}">
      <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding LayoutKeystrokeMeter.Label}" Classes="body" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                   Text="{Binding LayoutKeystrokeMeter.Caption}"
                   Classes="monoValue"
                   Classes.statusWarning="{Binding LayoutKeystrokeMeter.IsOverBudget}"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center" />
      </Grid>

      <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" IsVisible="{Binding HasSlots}">
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding MacroLengthMeter.Label}" Classes="body" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                   Text="{Binding MacroLengthMeter.Caption}"
                   Classes="monoValue"
                   Classes.statusWarning="{Binding MacroLengthMeter.IsOverBudget}"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center" />
      </Grid>

      <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding MacroCountMeter.Label}" Classes="body" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                   Text="{Binding MacroCountMeter.Caption}"
                   Classes="monoValue"
                   Classes.statusWarning="{Binding MacroCountMeter.IsOverBudget}"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center" />
      </Grid>
    </StackPanel>
  </Grid>
</UserControl>
